{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>And his wife looked back from behind him, and she became a pillar of salt.</b> It is possible to interpret 'from behind him' as referring to the overturning angel, concerning whom it is written above, ויהפך — 'and He overturned,' for he is the one who overturns, raining brimstone and fire from HaShem out of heaven; and therefore she was stricken with a pillar of salt, which comes from the power of the fire. And what Moses mentioned (Deuteronomy 29) — אשר הפך ה' — 'which HaShem overturned' — therefore it says, באפו ובחמתו — 'in His wrath and in His fury,' and this is the angel called אף וחמה — 'wrath and fury.'" "<b>And she became a pillar of salt.</b> The sage R. Abraham ibn Ezra wrote: ותהי הארץ — 'and the earth became.' And by way of the Midrash (razal): ותהי — 'his wife.' And so in the Midrash: a poor man came to her door to ask her for salt, and she did not wish to give him; and on account of this she was punished measure for measure — she sinned with salt and was stricken with a pillar of salt."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:13:40.291030713Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}